Error [E1302]: `option` expects 3 arguments (name, help, metavar), got 2
  --> tests/ui/args_spec_bad_option_arity.jet:4:25
    |
  4 |     spec :: args.spec().option("output", "write to FILE")
    |                         ^^^^^^
 Why: `ArgsSpec.option(name, help, metavar)` registers a value option like `--output FILE`
 Fix: pass three strings: the option name, a help description, and a metavar like `FILE`

Error [E0108]: argument 1 to `.parse()` should be String (text), not [String]
  --> tests/ui/args_spec_bad_option_arity.jet:5:29
    |
  5 |     parsed :: spec.parse(io.args()) ?? panic("parse failed")
    |                             ^^^^
 Why: built-in methods need arguments of the right type
 Fix: put the value in text with interpolation: "{x}"

Error [E0311]: `option` isn't a method on this value
  --> tests/ui/args_spec_bad_option_arity.jet:6:18
    |
  6 |     print(parsed.option("output") ?? "none")
    |                  ^^^^^^
 Why: only struct and enum values have instance methods
 Fix: check the spelling of `option`
